<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Sieradz</h1><p class="st-meta">1263 CE – 1339 CE (approx.) · capital Sieradz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Piast duchy in central Poland, a stepping stone for Leszek the Black and Wladyslaw the Elbow-high on their way to Krakow.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sieradz, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warta">Warta</a>, was part of the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-kuyavia">Casimir I of Kuyavia</a>. In the early 1260s his eldest son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-black">Leszek the Black</a> received it as his own duchy, which he kept after his father's death in 1267.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It was a farming land on the borders of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-greater-poland">Greater Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-silesia">Silesia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-black">Leszek the Black</a> used it as a base to become duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Krakow</a> in 1279, and later his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-i-lokietek">Wladyslaw I the Elbow-high</a> held Sieradz as he fought for the reunification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Its towns were developed under German law in the 13th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 1320 Sieradz remained a duchy within the reunited kingdom, held by Przemysl, a nephew of the king. When he died in 1339 it was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-poland-1025-1385">Kingdom of Poland</a> (1025-1385) and later became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sieradz-voivodeship">Sieradz Voivodeship</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-sieradz.jpg" alt="Duchy of Sieradz" width="320" height="280"><figcaption>Image: recoloured by Ulamm 23:50, 15 November 2007 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polska_WladLokietka_(1275-1300).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1263 CE – 1339 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sieradz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leszek the Black, Wladyslaw I the Elbow-high, Przemysl of Sieradz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sieradz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1301&amp;focus=duchy-of-sieradz" aria-label="Duchy of Sieradz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5104 392 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Sieradz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5424 648L5432 635M5424 648L5457 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5432 635h0M5457 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5424 648h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5424 648h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sieradz. <a href="/atlas?year=1301&amp;focus=duchy-of-sieradz">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
